17:T91d,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is message match on a landing page?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Message match is the degree of continuity between the ad copy and the landing page headline. A visitor who clicked an ad for 'free landing page audit' and arrives at a page that says 'Conversion optimization platform' has to re-evaluate whether they're in the right place. That re-evaluation costs time and conversions. Strong message match means the page headline immediately confirms the ad promise."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does message match affect Quality Score?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Google Ads Quality Score includes a landing page experience component that evaluates relevance between the keyword, ad, and landing page content. A high message match - ad keyword appears in the landing page H1, title tag, and meta description - improves Quality Score, which reduces CPC and improves ad placement."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How closely should the landing page headline match the ad?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The core promise should match within 3 words. If the ad says 'free landing page audit', the H1 should contain 'landing page audit'. The exact phrasing can vary, but the central value claim - what the visitor gets - must be immediately recognizable from the ad they clicked."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between keyword match and message match?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keyword match is an ad targeting setting. Message match is a landing page design principle. You can have perfect keyword targeting (ad shown to exactly the right searcher) and terrible message match (page headline ignores the keyword entirely). They are independent variables. Message match failures waste correctly targeted clicks."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I audit my own message match?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Read your ad copy, then immediately look at your landing page H1. Ask: does this H1 confirm the promise I made in the ad? Then check: does the page CTA match the CTA in the ad? Finally: is the audience the ad addressed the same audience the page headline speaks to? Three mismatches = three separate conversion failures."}}]}7:["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Article\",\"headline\":\"Landing Page Message Match: Ad-to-Page Alignment and Quality Score\",\"description\":\"Diagnostic guide for landing page message match failures - keyword mismatch, offer mismatch, audience mismatch, tone mismatch, visual mismatch, and CTA commitment mismatch between ad and page.\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Nebula Components\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Nebula Components\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://nebulacomponents.com/landing-page-message-match\"}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$17"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://nebulacomponents.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Landing Page Message Match\",\"item\":\"https://nebulacomponents.com/landing-page-message-match\"}]}"}}],"$L18"],null,"$L19"]}]
